   "reason": "The key on the king's diagonal is usually defended, which makes the bishop capture suicide; with the shield up she takes it anyway, absorbs the recapture, keeps the capture-stun and takes the king on the next move. | The army's capture priority is the mark, not the ally, so a Decoy laid the same turn the queen appears buys her the two or three turns her clock is worth — and any friendly fire on the mark is itself a capture-stun on the king.",
